module examples.err_layout_array_not_runtime

# plans/M10.md item A2, 03-hardware.md §3.1: the fixed-length array field is
# introduced as "one allowance the other three kinds do not have", so it is
# scoped to `runtime` by the same sentence that grants it. A `wire` layout
# with an array field is rejected by name.
#
# By name, and not with "has no exact byte size" — which would be false.
# `[u32; 4]` has a perfectly exact size on every target; a `wire` layout
# simply may not have one, and a diagnostic that gave the wrong reason
# would send an author looking for a sizing problem that does not exist.
# (`err-layout-no-exact-size` pins the case where the reason really is the
# absent size.)

@layout(wire, endian=big)
struct Header:
    magic: u32
    words: [u32; 4]
